        {
          "id": "derive-1-2",
          "claim": "The set $C = \\{\\aleph_n : n \\in \\omega\\}$ exists by Replacement, is contained in $\\aleph_\\omega$ and is cofinal in it, since $\\aleph_\\omega = \\bigcup C$ by [L3] means every $\\zeta \\in \\aleph_\\omega$ lies in some $\\aleph_n$ and hence satisfies $\\zeta \\le \\aleph_n$; moreover $n \\mapsto \\aleph_n$ is injective by the strict increase in [L3], so $C \\approx \\omega$ and $\\lvert C\\rvert = \\aleph_0$ by [L7]. [L3, L7, L9]",
