          "id": "derive-1-3",
          "claim": "Setting up claim (b): let $\\lambda = \\aleph_\\alpha$, $\\kappa = \\aleph_{\\alpha+1}$, and suppose $\\beta = \\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa) < \\kappa$, with $g : \\beta \\to \\kappa$ strictly increasing and cofinal by [L2]; then $\\kappa$ is a limit ordinal by [L4], so $\\beta$ is an infinite cardinal by [L1], and $\\beta \\le \\lambda$ because $\\beta$ is a cardinal below the least cardinal strictly above $\\lambda$ ([L3]); moreover $\\kappa = \\bigcup\\{g(\\xi) : \\xi \\in \\beta\\}$, since for $\\zeta \\in \\kappa$ the ordinal $\\zeta \\cup \\{\\zeta\\}$ also lies in $\\kappa$ and is $\\le g(\\xi)$ for some $\\xi$, putting $\\zeta \\in g(\\xi)$. [L1, L2, L3, L4, L9]",
