          "claim": "Claim (c): step 1.2 and [L1] give $\\operatorname{cf}(\\aleph_\\omega) \\le \\aleph_0$; and $\\aleph_\\omega$ is an infinite cardinal, hence a limit ordinal by [L4], so $\\operatorname{cf}(\\aleph_\\omega)$ is an infinite cardinal and $\\aleph_0 \\le \\operatorname{cf}(\\aleph_\\omega)$ by [L1] and [L4]; therefore $\\operatorname{cf}(\\aleph_\\omega) = \\aleph_0 < \\aleph_\\omega$ by the strict increase in [L3], and $\\aleph_\\omega$ is singular. [step 1.2, L1, L3, L4]",
          "step": "2.1",
