          "id": "derive-1-1",
          "claim": "Apply [L2] to the rule sending a function $h$ whose domain is an ordinal to $\\aleph_{\\bigcup \\operatorname{ran}(h)}$, which is given by a formula; this yields exactly one class function $T$, defined at every ordinal, with $T(\\beta) = \\aleph_{\\bigcup \\operatorname{ran}(T \\restriction \\beta)}$, and in particular $T(0) = \\aleph_{\\bigcup \\varnothing} = \\aleph_0$. [L1, L2, L5]",
