67:[L4] $\lvert X\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, equinumerous sets receive the same one, and $\lvert \alpha\rvert = \alpha$ exactly when $\alpha$ is a cardinal ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-cardinal]], [[def-equinumerous]]); assuming the Axiom of Choice every set has a cardinality ([[thm-well-ordering-theorem]]).
