97-
98:### F-A1 — `fs-cardinal-exponentiation-is-strictly-monotone-in-the-base`: APPROVED as proposed
99-
100-**Verified from disk.** Statement explanation (line ~47): "strictness does hold in
101-the other slot, where $\kappa < 2^{\kappa}$ at every cardinal". Remark: "so does
102-strictness in the exponent slot in the one case proved on this page, $\kappa < 2^{\kappa}$."
103-Both present verbatim.
104-
105-**The defect is real.** Strict monotonicity in the exponent slot is
106-$\mu<\nu \Rightarrow a^{\mu} < a^{\nu}$ for fixed base $a$. Cantor's inequality
107-compares $\kappa$ with $2^{\kappa}$ and is not an instance of it. Independently,
108-exponent-slot strictness is *false*: $1^{\mu} = 1 = 1^{\nu}$ for all $\mu<\nu$,
109-and $2^{\aleph_0} = 2^{\aleph_1}$ is consistent with ZFC — so the page asserts as
110-established a claim that is refutable and independent. `thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor`
111-clause (b) on disk reads exactly "$\kappa < 2^{\kappa}$" and claims nothing about
112-monotonicity, so the citation is also imprecise.
113-
114-**Approved text: both replacements exactly as the Beta proposed.** They are
115-minimal, true, and the Refutation is untouched.
116-
117-### T-A1..A5 — topology ambient-invariance: APPROVED, three sites as proposed, two AMENDED
118-
119-**Verified from disk.** All five sentences present verbatim at the cited lines.
120-
121-**The defect is real.** "A set compact in one ambient space is compact in every
122-other one in which it sits as a subspace" is false under its natural reading:
123-$[0,1]$ is compact in $\mathbb{R}$ and not compact in $\mathbb{R}$ with the
124-discrete topology, and both are ambients in which it sits as a subspace. The
125-Beta's own witness (infinite $A$, indiscrete vs discrete) is equally good. What is
126-intrinsic is compactness of the *space* $(A,\mathcal{T}_A)$, hence invariance
127-under homeomorphism — not compactness of a bare set under every induced topology.
128-`lem-compactness-of-a-subspace-is-ambient`'s Statement and proof are correct for
129-one fixed ambient; only the extrapolations are defective.
130-
131-**Approved as proposed:** `def-compact-space:63`, `rem-compactness-conventions-and-choice-ledger:58`,
132-`fs-a-compact-subset-is-closed-in-every-space:77`.
133-
134-**AMENDED — two proposals introduce a new falsehood and must not be applied as
135-written.** Both say a different ambient gives the same answer **"only when"** it
136-induces the same topology. That is a necessity claim and it is false: on an
137-infinite set the indiscrete and cofinite topologies are different and both
138-compact. The intended content is sufficiency. Apply these instead:
139-
140-- `items/lem-compactness-of-a-subspace-is-ambient.md:94` — replace
141-  "it is the reason compactness of `A` does not depend on which space `A` is regarded as sitting inside"
142-  with: "it shows that compactness can be checked using ambient open sets for this
143-  fixed induced topology. Another ambient is guaranteed to give the same answer
144-  when it induces the same topology on $A$; if the induced topology changes, the
145-  answer may change."
146-- `library/topology/compactness.md:36` — replace
147-  "That is a statement about the subspace alone, so the notion does not depend on which larger space the subset is regarded as sitting in"
148-  with: "That is a statement about the topological subspace, so it is invariant
149-  under homeomorphism. For the same underlying set in another ambient, the answer
150-  is guaranteed to agree when the induced topology agrees."
151-
152-**Additional constraint on `fs-a-compact-subset-is-closed-in-every-space:77`:** the
153-replacement is a clause inside a longer sentence that continues ", that being the
154-content of the intrinsic definition ([[def-compact-space]]), and a closed subset…".
155-Apply it so the sentence stays grammatical and **retains the `[[def-compact-space]]`
156-citation**, e.g.: "A compact subset remains compact in any other ambient inducing
157-the same topology on it — in particular, compactness is invariant under
158-homeomorphism — that being the content of the intrinsic definition
159-([[def-compact-space]]), and a closed subset of a compact space is still compact
160-([[thm-closed-subspace-of-a-compact-space-is-compact]])."
161-
162-All five sites are judge-visible material changes: stale `verification.judge` and
163-obsolete `audited` stamps come off, and Beta writes no replacement certification.
