180-  an ordinal is part of the definition.
181-- Step 1.1 concludes "so $n$ is a cardinal" and step 1.2 concludes "so $\omega$ is
182-  a cardinal". Their tag lists are [L1, L2, L4] and [L1, L4]; none of those states
183-  that $n$ or $\omega$ is an ordinal. Both steps establish only the
184-  no-smaller-equinumerous-ordinal half.
185-- `lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal` clause **(ii)** states exactly the missing
186-  premise: "every natural number is an ordinal ([[def-ordinal]]), and $\omega$ is
187-  an ordinal". That is [L3]'s first two clauses.
