      "claim": "Let $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$ and suppose $\\alpha \\in n$ with $\\alpha \\approx n$; then $\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{N}$ by [L2], so $\\alpha = n$ by [L1], giving $n \\in n$, which [L4] forbids; so $n$ is a cardinal. [L1, L2, L4]",
      "step": "1.1",
      "inputs": [
