        "L8",
        "L9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "derive-1-4",
      "claim": "For $m, n \\in \\mathbb{N}$ the sets $\\{0\\} \\times m$ and $\\{1\\} \\times n$ are finite and disjoint with $\\lvert \\{0\\} \\times m\\rvert = m$ and $\\lvert \\{1\\} \\times n\\rvert = n$ by [L6], so [L7] gives that $m \\sqcup n$, $m \\times n$ and ${}^{n}m$ are all finite, with finite cardinalities $m +_{\\mathbb{N}} n$, $m \\cdot_{\\mathbb{N}} n$ and $m^{n}$ respectively. [L6, L7, L9]",
